The file writers store unstructured meshes directly as VTU, VTKHDF, HDF5
with XDMF metadata, or NetCDF. A snapshot contains points, cell connectivity
and named point or cell fields; a time-series index records its time stamp.
See @ref tarch_plotting for the writer interfaces.

# Reading snapshots

ParaView reads the VTK and XDMF outputs. The scripts in `postprocessing/`
read every supported writer format through `solution_io.py`.
`render_solution.py` selects a field and renders its values;
`render_curve.py` colours a 2D mesh by the `Subdomain` cell field and joins
cell centres in snapshot order.

# Adaptive meshes

A coarse face can adjoin several fine faces, so the output mesh can be
non-conforming. Discontinuous point fields can also carry different values
at coincident coordinates. A visualisation filter that requires a continuous
field needs an explicit interpolation or resampling step.

*/
